  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1259 AM MDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nVery similar high temperatures are expected on Monday as they are on \nSunday, so we'll have to determine if we are going to issue another \nHeat Advisory during the forecast packages tomorrow. A little bit \nmore moisture is expected on Monday, so perhaps a few more heavy \nraining thunderstorms across the region, but the predominant impact \nis expected to be gusty outflow winds once again. \n\nOne more hot day on Tuesday with thunderstorm coverage increasing \nonce again - another Heat Advisory will be possible. By Wednesday \nthe upper level high pressure is pushed to the SE, which will allow \nfor all the built up monsoonal moisture to west to propagate to the \neast and for the main monsoon plume to move east, which will \nequate to more widespread showers and thunderstorms. There are \nelevated concerns for flash flooding over the Aspen Acres and 24\nburn scars and over urban areas. As the week continues there \nwill be a risk for flash flooding over areas with saturated \nsoils.",
